---
import HelpSection from "../../components/HelpSection.astro"
import Help from "../../layouts/Help.astro"
---

<Help
    title="Using Rollport"
    description="Choose what to import and how files are named, stop and continue an import, and import again later."
>
    <div class="max-w-(--container-text)">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Using Rollport</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-muted text-pretty">
            What you can change, and what happens on the next import.
        </p>
    </div>

    <HelpSection
        id="options"
        screen="options"
        alt="Rollport with Options open: date taken, media types, and file names"
    >
        <p>
            Open <b>Options</b> at the bottom of the window:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <b>Date taken</b>: any date, the last 7 or 30 days, the last 12
                months, or between two dates you choose.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>Media types</b>: all media, no Live Photo videos (the short
                clip that goes with each Live Photo), photos only, or videos
                only.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>File names</b>: can be set until the folder's first import.
                See <a href="#file-names">How files are named</a>.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection id="file-names">
        <p>
            Until a folder's first import, you can choose how its files are
            named:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Date and time in the name:{" "}
                <code>2026-09-02_15-04-11_IMG_0001.HEIC</code>
            </li>
            <li>
                Year and month folders: <code>2026/09/IMG_0001.HEIC</code>
            </li>
            <li>
                The phone's own name: <code>IMG_0001.HEIC</code>
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            After the first import, the folder keeps that naming, so all its
            files are named the same way.
        </p>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection
        id="copying"
        screen="importing"
        alt="Rollport is 63 percent done, with about a minute left"
    >
        <p>
            The photos go past as they are copied, and Rollport shows the time
            left. You can click <b>Stop</b> at any time: what is already copied
            stays in the folder, and the next import goes on from there.
        </p>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection
        id="again"
        screen="done"
        alt="Rollport says Imported 312, and that nothing was deleted from the iPhone"
    >
        <p>
            When the import is done, you can unplug the iPhone. Next time,
            connect it and click <b>Import</b>: only what is new is copied.
        </p>
        <p>
            The folder keeps a record of what it already has, in a small file
            named <code>rollport-library.db</code>. Keep that file, or the next
            import copies everything again.
        </p>
        <p>
            Rollport never deletes anything on the iPhone. Once the photos are
            in the folder, you can delete them on the iPhone yourself to free up
            space.
        </p>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection id="folders">
        <p>
            You can import into as many folders as you like. Each folder keeps
            its own record, so each one gets only what it does not have yet.
        </p>
    </HelpSection>
</Help>
